{
  "_comment": "ghost de-slop pattern config. Single source of truth for the scanner, the PreToolUse hook and the /ghost command. Edit allowlist to permit legit domain terms. Move a category between file_block_categories and file_warn_categories to change strictness without touching code.",
  "_comment_scope": "scan_extensions is the whole gate for the PreToolUse hook, and it lists only the formats a client document leaves in. Markdown is excluded on purpose: .md here is internal (notes, READMEs, plans, skills), and a block costs a full rewrite. Adding .md back reintroduces that cost. /ghost and ghost_scan.py on the command line scan any file you point them at, extension included. The hook is not the only automatic gate: skills/client-deliverable/assets/build_docx.js runs ghost_scan.py on its --in markdown and refuses to build a dirty source, which is what covers a .docx written through Bash rather than the Write tool.",
  "scan_extensions": [".txt", ".docx", ".pdf"],
  "skip_path_substrings": ["/.claude/ghost/", "/node_modules/", "/.git/", "/_archive", "/_archive-superseded", "/skills/", "/agents/", "/memory/"],
  "file_block_categories": ["dashes", "phrases", "buzzwords"],
  "file_warn_categories": [],
  "chat_warn_categories": ["dashes", "phrases"],
  "bypass_token": "ghost:allow",
  "dashes": ["—", "–", "―"],
  "phrases": [
    "\\bdelv(e|es|ing|ed)\\b",
